{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 1 EXECUTE IN PROGRESS (28 remaining issues, REB-1861 held for last).\n\nOrder: ascending by Jira comment count, canary REB-341 already done and verified.\n\nPer issue the script does, in order: paginated fetch -> completeness gate (fetched == reported total, refuse on mismatch) -> homogeneous bot-accountId check -> full backup written to backup/<KEY>.json BEFORE any DELETE -> keep-oldest-per-distinct-normalized-body deletion -> post-deletion re-fetch verification.\n\nVerified PASS so far: REB-341 (83->32), REB-190 (109->23), REB-427 (110->28) — each with missing_bodies=[] and unmarked count unchanged. REB-3271 and REB-3251 were no-ops (1 comment each).\n\nOperational note: Jira Cloud rate-limits this account at ~4 DELETE/s irrespective of client concurrency. The script's own 429/Retry-After-honouring wrapper has absorbed every rate-limit response (42 backoffs so far, 0 failed deletions) — this is exactly the failure mode the plan flagged, since delete_comment/_direct_rest_delete would have hard-aborted on the first 429. Estimated ~2h for the remaining ~29.5k deletions.\n\nAn interrupted run was resumed cleanly mid-REB-190: the restart recomputed the plan from live state (65 comments remaining), deleted 42, and verified 23/23 distinct bodies intact — confirming the resumability property."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787255438117869001,"uuid":"8495cb6c-1c0b-4d85-874e-69c809084f69"}